# Shot list — "The Little Match Girl"

20 shots (1–12, 13a, 13b, 14–19) + end title, 1280×720, 24 fps. The editor's animatic/EDL owns the timeline; times and durations here are targets (each shot generated at 4–10 s, trimmed in the edit). Script lines refer to `direction/script.md`.
"STREET" palette = cold indigo / slate blue / snow white, moonless dusk, warm window light only as small accents. "VISION" palette = amber, gold, candle-orange, deep warm shadow. "DAWN" palette = pale grey-blue with a faint rose sky.

Continuity anchors (all shots): the GIRL (design sheet from production-designer), the CORNER (the nook where two house fronts meet, one standing further out than the other; a rough plastered wall she strikes matches on), the STREET, the GRANDMOTHER. From shot 6 to shot 17 the girl is in the SAME corner, in the same pose family, with the same wall behind her; visions appear in or through that wall and return to it.

